{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "speaker": "hayes",
   "text": "Last one. Chris, September twenty-ninth, eleven-oh-one in the morning, on the record. Quote... Too much smoke on a Robertson move for there not to be fire. We were all a year too late.",
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 11.92
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "speaker": "odog",
   "text": "Nick Robertson trade rumours. The most reliable smoke in hockey. It shows up every October... like the leaves.",
   "start": 11.92,
   "end": 19.679
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "speaker": "hayes",
   "text": "Justin's reply, nine minutes later. You have some insider news, Elliott?",
   "start": 19.679,
   "end": 24.799,
   "hl": [
    "justin"
   ]
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "speaker": "odog",
   "text": "Friedman over here. Only Chris put his name on it... and I notice he didn't put a DATE on it.",
   "start": 24.799,
   "end": 31.2
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "speaker": "hayes",
   "text": "Only Chris weighed in.",
   "start": 31.2,
   "end": 32.96,
   "hl": [
    "chris"
   ]
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "speaker": "hayes",
   "text": "And on July first... Robertson was traded to Pittsburgh. For a twenty twenty-eight fourth.",
   "start": 32.96,
   "end": 38.56,
   "reveal": true
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "speaker": "odog",
   "text": "Ten months late, for a FOURTH. But there was no clock on it, Hayesy. You can't lose a take with no clock on it. Fire is fire.",
   "start": 38.56,
   "end": 47.12
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "speaker": "hayes",
   "text": "Chris takes the W... unless the Marshal wants to argue the calendar. Nobody else was in the room for it.",
   "start": 47.12,
   "end": 53.76,
   "final": true
  }
 ],
